[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2528372991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100162#issuecomment-2528372991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100162","id":2528372991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ws-j_","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-09T15:29:15Z","updated_at":"2024-12-09T15:29:15Z","body":"> * I suggest renaming the Measure tool to Ruler (also with its internal enum name), so that it matches the name in the 2D editor. This should also be done for the shortcut name.\r\n\r\nDone.\r\n\r\n> * Draw the distance text with a black outline and use the bold editor font with a _slightly_ increased font size. Doing this will help a lot with visibility on mixed-color backgrounds, which can be an issue right now:sin\r\nitor for reference:\r\n\r\nDone.\r\n\r\n> * Display a the unique with a `m` suffix for \"meters\" (e.g. `123.456 m`), as 3D units are meters in Godot.\r\n\r\nDone.\r\n\r\n\r\n> * Round the display to 3 decimals using `String.pad_decimals()`, so there's always 3 decimals displayed (even if technically not needed in some cases). This prevents the text from jumping around as the ruler moves.\r\n\r\nDone.\r\n\r\n> * The ruler line occasionally disappears depending on which direction it's going towards:\r\n\r\nI can't reproduce this. Does the target mesh have a collision node associated with it? At the moment the end points snap to only collisions, since snapping to geometry is a different animal.\r\n\r\n> * You could look into replicating the rectangle and angle measurements from the 2D ruler in the 3D ruler, but this can be left for a future PR.\r\n\r\nWill probably save this for another PR since there is a lot of different avenues this kind of functionality can take. Persisting measurements, more than one measurement on the screen, measuring volume, angles, etc. I think it makes sense to wait for feedback from the public on this initial step.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2528372991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2528398917","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100162#issuecomment-2528398917","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100162","id":2528398917,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WtE5F","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-09T15:34:44Z","updated_at":"2024-12-09T15:34:44Z","body":"See video below:\r\n\r\nIn one instance the line does go behind the mesh and extends depth-wise in the viewport, but this is expected.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2e2f09d6-3d8a-46b2-8a4a-34884a00ebd0\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2528398917/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2528556859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100162#issuecomment-2528556859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100162","id":2528556859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Wtrc7","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"